<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=typewriter">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Communication and computing</p><h1 class="enc-title">Typewriter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1865">1865</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The typewriter is a mechanical or electromechanical machine that prints characters on paper when a key is pressed, a type element striking an inked ribbon against the page. Its invention was incremental: Rasmus Malling-Hansen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> invented the Hansen Writing Ball in 1865, and it went into commercial production in 1870 as the first typewriter sold. The first commercially successful model was patented in 1868 by Christopher Latham Sholes and others in Milwaukee, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a>, and made by E. Remington and Sons from 1873 with the QWERTY layout, still the standard for English computer keyboards. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/personal-computer">Personal computers</a> largely replaced typewriters after the 1980s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/typewriter.jpg" alt="Typewriter" width="330" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GodeNehler · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MEK_II-371.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>1865</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Denmark</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd>Rasmus Malling-Hansen · Christopher Latham Sholes</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Historians estimate that some form of typewriter was invented 52 times: a British patent of 1714 granted to Henry Mill appears to describe a similar machine, and Pellegrino Turri built one for a blind friend between 1801 and 1808.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=typewriter">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
